`,r.jsx(u.p,{children:"The course walks through building Android apps from scratch using Jetpack Compose and the Kotlin programming language."}),`
`,r.jsx(u.p,{children:"So far, I have completed the first unit of this course, where I learned how to create a simple Android app with a user interface that displays images and text. I also got more comfortable with Kotlin’s syntax, which feels a lot like TypeScript, so it clicked pretty quickly for me. After that I set up Android Studio and created my very first project. This helped me get familiar with the IDE, Android’s project structure, and how to use Composable functions to display UI elements like text and images, arranged in layouts like columns, rows, and boxes. The best part was finally emulating the project on a virtual device and seeing my first Android app come to life!"}),`
